<title>FINLAND: Merita proposes top staff options scheme.</title>
<headline>Merita proposes top staff options scheme.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish banking group Merita Oy said in a statement on Tuesday it would propose to the annual general meeting a 1.70 million markka options scheme for about 100 management-level employees.</p>
<p>The warrants would entitle holders to subscribe at most 17.0 million Merita shares. Subscriptions could be made between March 1, 2000 and March 31, 2003. The subscription price would be the weighted average price of Merita's A share on the Helsinki bourse March 10-14, 1997, Merita said.</p>
</text>
